# Pure Press frontend configuration.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` in this folder if you need to change anything.
# Create React App reads REACT_APP_* values when it BUILDS, not when the page is
# opened, so a change needs a restart of `npm start` or a new `npm run build`.
# Everything here is optional; see docs/engineering/configuration.md.

# Where the API lives. Leave this unset in the usual setups:
#   - on localhost the app calls http://localhost:5000
#   - on any *.onrender.com address it calls https://news-curator-deployed.onrender.com
#
# Set it only for a backend somewhere else. Mind the two shapes the code expects
# today: src/services/api.js (and the Check Anything page that reads it) wants
# the address WITH the /api suffix, while ArticlePage, LoginPage and SignupPage
# want the bare server address. Until the app reads one shared value, setting it
# breaks one group or the other, which is why it is commented out.
# REACT_APP_API_URL=https://your-backend.example.com
